  "notes": "R&B-and-gospel-inflected country with a pop-crossover tail — groove-forward, low-tempo, vocally agile. The tempo band is the entry's own headline: \"BPM 72–107 straight on 2&4 — a strikingly narrow and slow band,\" so the ceiling sits below the genre's mode. Drums are \"a hip-hop-derived pocket — programmed clap/snap on the backbeat, 16th hats, a short sampled kick on 1 and 'and-of-3,' tambourine on chorus 8ths, and live cymbal overdubs. Half-time verses opening to straight choruses,\" which is the 3& secondary kick anchor, a snap layer on the snare and a `fullTimeVariantProb` carrying the verse-to-chorus switch. Harmony is the gospel claim taken literally: \"I–IV–V with gospel IV–iv–I borrows, I–V–vi–IV, and a static I7 vamp on the groove cuts\" — the IV–iv–I borrow is a family, the static I7 vamp is the raised seventh share plus a `vamp` weight. The keyboard-first harmony is documented through the producer — \"Rhodes/Wurlitzer and organ carry the harmony\" — so the chord voicing sits lower and closer than the genre's guitar-shaped default. Melody is \"mid-alto with blues bends, pentatonic runs and real melisma — the most agile female melodic writing in the modern cohort.\" ⚠ The synth sub is described alongside an electric bass that \"is a melodic voice on the groove cuts,\" i.e. reinforcement rather than the low end, so no `drums.bass808` block is authored and the live bass is kept. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the snap offsets, the full-time variant share and the counter ratio.",
